00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:06.840
Leah: As we discussed previously, Pair programming is where
two people within a team collaborate and work as a pair.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.110
So how is this different to Mob programming?

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.490
With Mob programming the ‘whole team’
works together involving several people.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:21.119
In this instance the roles of ‘Driver’ and
‘Navigator[s]’ would rotate between the

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.550
programmers, and the roles would switch frequently.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:30.020
One person, the Driver would always write
the code and the other[s] would observe the

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.579
code identifying errors and problem solving.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.410
Both Pair and Mob programming practices are
especially useful for sharing knowledge.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:44.620
So, what are the advantages and
disadvantages of Pair programming?

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:44.762
Chris: Advantages

00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:51.821
Pair programming helps to decrease software errors, it
is a less formal review process, and unexpected items

00:00:51.822 --> 00:00:54.962
would be noticed quicker from Navigator or Observer.

00:00:55.602 --> 00:01:00.482
It helps to improve software quality and
has a ‘positive impact’ on the source code.

00:01:01.001 --> 00:01:06.652
It reduces the ‘risk’ of a project especially
if a team member leaves, and experts on specific

00:01:06.652 --> 00:01:11.412
subjects can share knowledge with team which
could help to increase the productivity.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:16.572
It can also help to integrate a new team
member who may have problems with the source

00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:18.922
code as they are unfamiliar with the system.

00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:25.481
It also helps with different ability levels as a
beginner programmer will increase their productivity

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.851
when paired with someone more experienced.

00:01:28.931 --> 00:01:36.702
Fatigue can decrease productivity therefore swapping
‘Driver and Navigator roles’ can also increase productivity.

00:01:37.482 --> 00:01:44.512
It can help with ‘better team cohesion’ reducing the rate
at which developers exit the team, and it has been found

00:01:44.602 --> 00:01:51.912
that pair programming stimulates focus, motivation, and
satisfaction, and is enjoyed for the social dimension.

00:01:53.132 --> 00:01:54.172
Leah: Disadvantages

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:59.821
It has been found that it is more useful for
‘complex projects’ but does not add value for

00:01:59.821 --> 00:02:03.232
smaller tasks which result in minor bug fixes.

00:02:03.812 --> 00:02:09.242
It may increase work time and decrease
productivity as more work hours are spent in pair

00:02:09.242 --> 00:02:11.962
programming rather than programming individually.

00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:20.442
Some developers need or prefer to work alone, especially
when new and needing to build up skills, confidence,

00:02:20.481 --> 00:02:23.571
and self-assurance from producing their own code.

00:02:24.582 --> 00:02:29.872
There is also a danger of personality conflict
which could in turn decrease productivity.

00:02:31.012 --> 00:02:38.101
It can be time-consuming to setup as communication
mechanisms, objectives, expectations of approach

00:02:38.172 --> 00:02:41.661
need to be shared, and continuous feedback is needed.

00:02:42.432 --> 00:02:47.292
The Project manager or Developer lead would
need to manage and identify which adjustments

00:02:47.322 --> 00:02:49.952
are necessary for the project to be successful.

00:02:51.161 --> 00:02:57.031
It may add extra cost to a project as more developer
pairs might be needed to meet tighter deadlines.

00:02:57.832 --> 00:03:04.161
Good communication processes and mechanisms in pair
programming are key, because if there are poor standards

00:03:04.192 --> 00:03:11.142
or programming practices, and unexpected errors,
code could become disorganised and may need a rework.

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:13.362
Chris: Mob programming

00:03:14.382 --> 00:03:18.192
As we have already discussed ‘Mob programming’
is similar to ‘Pair programming’ except

00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:20.832
there is one Driver and several Navigators.

00:03:21.552 --> 00:03:26.871
The main difference is that the team works together,
and this could include other tasks for the Navigator

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:33.841
roles such as ‘identifying stories’, ‘designing’,
‘testing’, and ‘deployment’ depending on the project.

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:35.332
Leah: Advantages

00:03:35.332 --> 00:03:39.660
It has been found that Mob programming
works well for complex software products.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:45.270
There is better ‘communication and
collaboration’, and the team is self-organised

00:03:45.419 --> 00:03:47.870
which works with modern Agile practices.

00:03:48.789 --> 00:03:54.920
There is also more ‘Team alignment’ with an ‘increase
in of shared knowledge’, this is especially so where the

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.550
team do not have a shared understanding of the project.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:04.849
Teams have found that mob programming can be fun and
interactive with an improvement of the learning experience.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:11.189
Mob programming done right can be ‘inclusive’, as
it can provide a safe and encouraging environment

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.810
for beginner programmers or new team members.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.630
Chris: Disadvantages

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:23.409
Effects of ‘dominant personalities’ could result in
conflict within a larger team, but also ‘Groupthink’

00:04:23.539 --> 00:04:29.300
can occur within a team, where the desire for
harmony results in poor unchallenged decisions.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:36.450
Mob programming could end up being ‘less productive’ as
it could be difficult to keep focus for the ‘co-pilots’

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.600
or ‘navigators’ who aren’t in possession of the keyboard.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:45.060
There could also be concerns of mangers about
the difficulty of having the whole team working

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.740
together for just one element of a project.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:54.500
Although considered a positive practice Mob programming
still needs more validation through research to

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.870
emphasise its benefits and reduce potential risks.

